                <pb facs="0779" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-16T18:00:00+00:00">January 16, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 16—2:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>20. The Counselor of the British Embassy called this afternoon to say that they
                    had received instructions from London to support any representations which we
                    might make to the French Government to secure their cooperation concerning
                    Liberian slavery situation. British Embassy indicated matter was very urgent as
                    it was to be referred to present session of Council of League of Nations.</p>
                <p>I informed him that no instructions had as yet been received in the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
